# Use /backend-development

When working on files matching this rule, you MUST use the project skill `/backend-development`.

1. Read `.cursor/skills/backend-development/SKILL.md` before writing or changing C#/.NET code.
2. Follow every workflow, critical, structure, formatting, data-access, and testing rule in that skill.
3. Do not skip the pause after service/endpoint/repository work: ask before any test changes.
4. Use EF Core only for data access. Do not add raw SQL.

If the skill file is missing, stop and tell the user instead of inventing conventions.